I want to categorize the given bank transactions.

Transactions to categorize:
{{#each transactions}}
---
Transaction ID: {{id}}
* Amount: {{amount}}
* Type: {{type}}
{{#if description}}
* Description: {{description}}
{{/if}}
* Payee: {{payee}}
{{#if date}}
* Date: {{date}}
{{/if}}
{{/each}}

Existing categories by group:
{{#each categoryGroups}}
GROUP: {{name}} (ID: "{{id}}")
{{#each categories}}
* {{name}} (ID: "{{id}}")
{{/each}}
{{/each}}

{{#if rules.length}}
Existing Rules:
{{#each rules}}
{{incIndex @index}}. {{ruleName}} → {{categoryName}}
   Conditions: {{#each conditions}}{{field}} {{op}} {{value}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

IMPORTANT: You MUST respond with ONLY a valid JSON ARRAY of objects, where each object corresponds to a categorized transaction from the list above. No other text is permitted. Use this structure for each object:
[
  {
    "transactionId": "string", // Must identically match the Transaction ID provided
    "type": "existing"{{#if suggestNewCategoriesEnabled}}|"new"{{/if}}|"rule",
    "categoryId": "string", // Required for existing category or rule match
    "ruleName": "string"{{#if suggestNewCategoriesEnabled}}, // Required if matching rule
    "newCategory": { // Required if suggesting new category
      "name": "string", 
      "groupName": "string",
      "groupIsNew": boolean
    }{{else}} // Required if matching rule{{/if}}
  }
]

DO NOT output any text before or after the JSON ARRAY. Your entire response must be a valid, parsable JSON ARRAY mapped exactly to every input transaction!

Examples of valid response array elements:
[
  {"transactionId": "id-1", "type": "existing", "categoryId": "abc123"},
  {"transactionId": "id-2", "type": "rule", "categoryId": "def456", "ruleName": "Coffee Shop"}{{#if suggestNewCategoriesEnabled}},
  {"transactionId": "id-3", "type": "new", "newCategory": {"name": "Pet Supplies", "groupName": "Pets", "groupIsNew": true}}{{/if}}
]

